From: JuggyMcNutty <11588877+JuggyMcNutty@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 22:09:50 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Lightmaps: light only the texels a light can reach

FORK ONLY. This project ships a NO-AI Code Rule asking that LLM-written
changes stay in a fork and are never PR'd upstream. These were written with
Claude. Do not submit them.

Every light's effect and contribution ran over every texel of the lightmap,
though all but the cylinder effect give exactly zero beyond the light's
radius. On Liberty Island a burning barrel (a dynamic light with the fire
waver effect, so it re-lights what it touches every frame) had twelve large
surfaces rebuilt per frame: ~300,000 texels walked for ~7 lights each, of
which ~550 texel-light pairs were in reach -- ~90 ms a frame on the TrimUI
Smart Pro.

LightmapBuilder::FindLitSpans now finds, per row, the texels within the
light's radius, and LightEffect::Run and AddLightContribution work on those
spans only. A row of texel positions is a line (CalcWorldLocations
interpolates between the row's ends), so the span is where that line is
inside the light's sphere, plus a texel of margin; a lightmap as a whole is
not an affine grid (its rows drift up to ~100 units from one), which is why
this is per row. Checked over Liberty Island: 0 of 3.1 million in-reach
texels outside a span, across 232,000 light passes. Static lights skip
Shadow.Load when nothing is in reach. Cylinder lights, and one-texel-wide
lightmaps, still cover everything.

The per-texel values are unchanged, save that a texel can now fall in a
vector loop's scalar tail or the other way round (rounding at 1e-7).
